  "query_preview": "..\nThe monsoon trough extending into Tropical Depression (TD) 26W will\nlift northward as 26W approaches the far northern CNMI through\nThursday. This will lead to increasing showers, convection, and winds\nfor the region. The zones were split as Saipan and Tinian are\nforecasted for numerous showers and strong southwesterlies with gale-\nforce gusts possible beginning Thursday night. Guam and Rota can \nexpect high-end (50%) scattered showers increasing to numerous \nshowers on Friday and fresh to strong southwesterlies with near gale-\nforce gusts possible. As of early this evening, a Flood Watch was \nnot issued as ensemble guidance significantly differs, showing the \nhigher ranges of rainfall totals over the far northern CNMI. However,\nflooding potentials will be re-evaluated with the next forecast \nperiod, so any hydrology product should not be ruled out. In \naddition, there is potential for a Wind Advisory this weekend for all\nthe Marianas as sustained winds of 30 to 39 mph are possible. As \ntime continues, this product may also be issued within the next few \nforecast periods. With the current forecast track, Saipan and Tinian \nwill most likely be included in a TS Watch with the next forecast \nupdate. As for next week, a dry spell may occur before showers \nincrease again late next week.",
